<<~ ahu #/entry>>

! Projection Loom

Projection Loom grows architecture from authored CAD-solid construction rules, verifies volumetric attachment before admitting evolutionary lineages, and casts one continuous object into multiple orthographic drawing views. Each project supplies the subject's construction genome and evidence; the loom governs contact, projection, selection, and isolated control-media export.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/invariants>>

!! Solid Construction and Lineage

* ''Grow from relation.'' The project names one material foundation and children with explicit parent attachment. Every new structure occupies measurable positive volume inside its supporting solid. Vertices and painted silhouettes do not invent support.
* ''One joined body.'' Every candidate admitted to final production resolves as one valid OpenCascade BRep solid. Zero-thickness touches, detached decorations, and interrupted attachment graphs fail the solid gate; exceptions require a separate scene object, never an implied member of the same architecture.
* ''Construction governs mutation.'' A genome changes bounded massing, tower spacing, gallery reach, brace sections, and other authored structural parameters. Each candidate regrows solid geometry. Tessellated projections serve as outputs, never as evolutionary genotype.
* ''Shared camera, multiple witnesses.'' Front, side, back, top, and oblique views project the same held solid under named orthographic cameras. An external mask or painting informs form and light without claiming unseen geometry.
* ''Ink follows engineering.'' Outline, occlusion, structural crease, material seam, and detail lines occupy separated controls. Semantic roles flow from named construction parts. Visual cleanup cannot disguise a failed joint.
* ''Ancestry through genomes.'' A selected construction genome re-enters the same growth grammar across epochs. Independent source references remain the fitness witness; self-produced masks stabilize lineages only at secondary weight.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/contract>>

!! Executable Carrier

`tools/projection-loom/` supplies the `projection-loom/solid-project/v2` project contract and the `projection-loom` CLI. `validate` inspects authored attachment volumes and the fused CAD body. `grow` exports a single STEP production solid, interchange geometry, a saved genome, and independent transparent drawing controls. `evolve` explores Sobol populations and progressively narrower lineages subject to the solid gate. `epoch-loop` repeats full constructive growth and feedback passes while returning approved genomes to the growth grammar.

Every emitted render derives from the CAD model. A STEP model or render transport mesh may be archived as evidence; subsequent growth resumes through the genome and authored construction rules, not vertex bending of exported geometry. The geometry gate warrants overlap and CAD validity, not physical load performance.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/ooda-ha>>

✶ observe the subject grammar, root mass, joint tolerances, view registration, and external reference evidence
⏿ orient every growing child toward its named supporting parent and the one shared orthographic coordinate frame
◇ select only candidates whose overlaps and fused solid meet the project's construction requirements
▶ grow solid volumes, evolve distinct lineages, verify joints, then cast separate silhouette, line, and light controls
↺ carry the chosen construction genome into further epochs without allowing rendered masks or exported meshes to masquerade as structural ancestry

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/edges>>

